{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1547439-sorcerer-and-saint-questions","id":1547439,"title":"Sorcerer and Saint Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-01T17:44:33-08:00","id":1547439,"title":"Sorcerer and Saint Questions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> New to Sorcerers and Saints in Scion:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Sorcerers can get Relics when buying Paraphernalia, do they get the Purview Innate Power of a Relic?</li> <li><s><i>IF</i> the answer to the first question is YES, can they also buy Boons?</s> No one can buy boons, so this question makes no sense anymore.</li> <li><i>IF</i> the answer to the first question is YES, what happens when a Sorcerer gets a relic that grants access to the Magic Purview?</li> <li>A Saint can also be a Sorcerer. But Saints have different rules for Callings and Purview access, which rules (or combination thereof ) are used for a Saint Sorcerer?</li> <li>If Saints do not have Legend, how do they get to Hero or Demigod Tier?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-04-2025, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T20:18:03-08:00","id":1547440,"title":"","content":"1. I <i>believe</i> that normally sorcerers can't access Purviews through Relics unless they are also another type of being that can, like a Scion who learned Techniques through the Magic Purview.<br /> 2. If you allow sorcerers to access Purviews through Relics, then yes, they can buy Boons.<br /> 3. If you allow sorcerers to access Purviews through Relics, then I'd allow them access to the Magic Purview. They don't get any extra Workings or Techniques from it, just the innate power, Marvels, and Boons.<br /> 4. The sidebar on p. 77, Denizens, Saints, and Sorcery explains this. Build a saint-sorcerer as a sorcerer, except they gain the saint's Cardinal Virtue mechanic, have a phantom Saint Calling rating determined by their tier, and can substitute Knacks for Techniques.<br /> 5. This is covered by the Culture Hero mechanic on p. 14. They still complete sets of short, long, and band deeds, and advance their Callings when they do so, and increase in tier at the same number of such advances as Scions do with Legend advances. If you prefer, picture a saints having a phantom Legend number that goes up on a full deed set but whose only effect is to count down to the next tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T22:55:54-08:00","id":1547445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1547439-sorcerer-and-saint-questions?p=1547440#post1547440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I <i>believe</i> that normally sorcerers can't access Purviews through Relics unless they are also another type of being that can, like a Scion who learned Techniques through the Magic Purview.<br /> 2. If you allow sorcerers to access Purviews through Relics, then yes, they can buy Boons.<br /> 3. If you allow sorcerers to access Purviews through Relics, then I'd allow them access to the Magic Purview. They don't get any extra Workings or Techniques from it, just the innate power, Marvels, and Boons.<br /> 4. The sidebar on p. 77, Denizens, Saints, and Sorcery explains this. Build a saint-sorcerer as a sorcerer, except they gain the saint's Cardinal Virtue mechanic, have a phantom Saint Calling rating determined by their tier, and can substitute Knacks for Techniques.<br /> 5. This is covered by the Culture Hero mechanic on p. 14. They still complete sets of short, long, and band deeds, and advance their Callings when they do so, and increase in tier at the same number of such advances as Scions do with Legend advances. If you prefer, picture a saints having a phantom Legend number that goes up on a full deed set but whose only effect is to count down to the next tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> More questions arise:<br /> <br /> 6. For point number 4, does it mean that a Saint Sorcerer gets a free Saint Knack at character creation?<br /> 7. For Sorcerers, and Sorcerer Saints, do new Workings gained at Legend 5, and 9, come with a free Technique (besides the Inherent Technique)?<br /> 8. Saint Sorcerers do get their Hero (Fated Exemplar) and Demigod (Fated Champion, World-Shaking Virtue, etc) qualities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-02-2025, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T06:42:55-08:00","id":1547513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1547439-sorcerer-and-saint-questions?p=1547440#post1547440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I <i>believe</i> that normally sorcerers can't access Purviews through Relics unless they are also another type of being that can, like a Scion who learned Techniques through the Magic Purview.<br /> 2. If you allow sorcerers to access Purviews through Relics, then yes, they can buy Boons.<br /> 3. If you allow sorcerers to access Purviews through Relics, then I'd allow them access to the Magic Purview. They don't get any extra Workings or Techniques from it, just the innate power, Marvels, and Boons.<br /> 4. The sidebar on p. 77, Denizens, Saints, and Sorcery explains this. Build a saint-sorcerer as a sorcerer, except they gain the saint's Cardinal Virtue mechanic, have a phantom Saint Calling rating determined by their tier, and can substitute Knacks for Techniques.<br /> 5. This is covered by the Culture Hero mechanic on p. 14. They still complete sets of short, long, and band deeds, and advance their Callings when they do so, and increase in tier at the same number of such advances as Scions do with Legend advances. If you prefer, picture a saints having a phantom Legend number that goes up on a full deed set but whose only effect is to count down to the next tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just thought again, my question 2 is totally wrong... No one can buy Boons, there is no cost for them anywhere, so the question makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T10:47:53-08:00","id":1548031,"title":"","content":"Hey! I hope I'm not derailing your thread, but I had a request to make some Sorcerer Sheets for Scion and I was wondering if y'all could check it out and see what you think so far.<br /> <br /> Some things to note:<br /> <br /> 1: It's not fully interactive yet, once I know the layout is good I'll finish the form fields.<br /> <br /> 2: This is a modded Origin sheet, but I did add a Legend rating and added more callings, since in the write up it mentioned Sorcerers needing Legend to claim a source of power. If you think I should add more Legend dots to this sheet though, let me know. Or if you think the mortal version should not have Legend let me know and I can remove it.<br /> <br /> 3: Once I have this base sheet ready, then I'll try to make some Mods for a Hero and Demigod version, assuming I can make room on those sheets for the new Sorcerer components.<br /> <br /> 4: I was a little fuzzy on Techniques (and spells and rituals I guess),and Charms, so the section I made for those on page 2 is kind of free form, which hopefully has enough room for what you might need to write up. If you think that needs work though, let me know what you might like to see.<br /> <br /> Anyway, let me know what you think so far. If you think it needs any adjustments, just let me know and I'll see what I can do. Hopefully it's ok so far t